<html ><head ><meta charset="UTF-8"  /><meta name="author" content="Martin Walther - @tinuwalther"  /><meta name="keywords" content="Pode, PSHTML, PowerShell, Mermaid Diagram"  /><meta name="description" content="Builds beatuifull HTML-Files with PSHTML from native PowerShell-Scripts"  /><link href="\assets\BootStrap\bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet"  /><link href="\assets\style\style.css" rel="stylesheet"  /><script src="\assets\BootStrap\bootstrap.bundle.min.js"  ></script><script src="\assets\Chartjs\Chart.bundle.min.js"  ></script><title >#PSXi Pode Server</title><link href="/assets/img/favicon.ico" rel="icon" type="image/x-icon"  /></head><Body ><header ><div Class="jumbotron text-center" Id="j1" Style="padding:15; background-color:#012456"  ><p ><h1 >#PSXi Pode Server</h1></p><p >I ♥ PS Pode > This is an example for using pode and PSHTML, requested by API. The page is 
$(if(Test-Path 'D:\github.com\PodePSHTML\views\Pode-Server.pode'){
    $($regex = '[0-9]{4}\-[0-9]{2}\-[0-9]{2}\s[0-9]{2}\:[0-9]{2}\:[0-9]{2}')
    $($index = Get-Content 'D:\github.com\PodePSHTML\views\Pode-Server.pode')
    $($created = Get-Date ([regex]::Match($index, $regex).Value))
    $($diffTime = New-TimeSpan -Start $created -End (Get-Date))
    $(if($diffTime.TotalMinutes -gt 60 -and $diffTime.TotalMinutes -lt 1440){
        # $badge = 'badge badge-warning' # Bootstrap v4.6.x
        $badge = 'badge text-bg-warning' # Bootstrap v5.3.x
    }elseif($diffTime.TotalMinutes -gt 1440){
        # $badge = 'badge badge-danger' # Bootstrap v4.6.x
        $badge = 'badge text-bg-danger' # Bootstrap v5.3.x
    }else{
        # $badge = 'badge badge-success' # Bootstrap v4.6.x 
        $badge = 'badge text-bg-success' # Bootstrap v5.3.x
    })
    $(span -class $badge {'{0} Days {1} Hours {2} Minutes' -f $diffTime.Days, $diffTime.Hours, $diffTime.Minutes})
})
 old.</p></div></header><Section Id="section"  ><nav Class="navbar navbar-expand-sm bg-dark navbar-dark sticky-top"  ><div Class="container-fluid"  ><a Target="_self" Class="navbar-brand" href="/"  >»HOME</a><button Class="navbar-toggler" data-bs-target="#collapsibleNavbar" data-bs-toggle="collapse" type="button"  ><span Class="navbar-toggler-icon"  ></span></button><div Class="collapse navbar-collapse" Id="collapsibleNavbar"  ><ul Class="navbar-nav"  ><li Class="nav-item dropdown"  ><button Class="nav-link dropdown-toggle btn btn-sm-outline" data-bs-toggle="dropdown" type="button"  >Pode</button><ul Class="dropdown-menu bg-dark navbar-dark"  ><li Class="dropdown-item bg-dark navbar-dark"  ><a Target="_self" Class="nav-link" href="#InstallPode"  >Install Pode</a></li><li Class="dropdown-item bg-dark navbar-dark"  ><a Target="_self" Class="nav-link" href="#ConfigurePode"  >Configure Pode</a></li><li Class="dropdown-item bg-dark navbar-dark"  ><a Target="_self" Class="nav-link" href="#StartPode"  >Start Pode</a></li></ul></li><li Class="nav-item"  ><a Class="nav-link" Target="_blank" href="https://badgerati.github.io/Pode/"  >Pode docs</a></li><li Class="nav-item"  ><a Target="_self" Class="nav-link" href="/help"  >Help</a></li></ul></div></div></nav><div Class="Container" Id="Content"  ><article Id="Pode"  ><h1 Style="color:#212529"  >Pode</h1><p Style="color:#000"  >Pode is a Cross-Platform framework to create web servers that host REST APIs, Web Sites, and TCP/SMTP Servers.</p><p Style="color:#000"  >It also allows you to render dynamic files using .pode files, which is effectively embedded PowerShell, or other Third-Party template engines. 
                            Pode also has support for middleware, sessions, authentication, and logging; as well as access and rate limiting features. 
                            There's also Azure Functions and AWS Lambda support!</p><p Style="color:#000"  >Pode and Pode.web is created by Matthew Kelly <a Target="_blank" href="https://github.com/Badgerati"  >(Badgerati)</a>, licensed under the MIT License.</p><h2 Id="InstallPode" Style="color:#212529"  >How to install pode</h2><p Style="color:#000"  >You can install pode from the PowerShell-Gallery.</p><pre Style="color:#000"  >Install-Module -Name Pode -Verbose</pre><h2 Id="ConfigurePode" Style="color:#212529"  >How to configure pode</h2><p Style="color:#000"  >Create a root folder, for example PodePSHTML:</p><pre Style="color:#000"  >New-Item -Path . -Name PodePSHTML -ItemType Directory -Force -Confirm:$false</pre><p Style="color:#000"  >Change in to the new directory:</p><pre Style="color:#000"  >Set-Location ./PodePSHTML</pre><p Style="color:#000"  >Clone the code from my repository:</p><pre Style="color:#000"  >git clone https://github.com/tinuwalther/PodePSHTML.git</pre><h2 Id="StartPode" Style="color:#212529"  >How to start pode</h2><p Style="color:#000"  >Open a PowerShell and enter:</p><pre Style="color:#000"  >pwsh ./PodePSHTML/PodeServer.ps1</pre></article></div></Section><pre Style="color:#000"  >Re-builds the page: I ♥ PS > Invoke-WebRequest -Uri http://localhost:8080/api/pode -Method Post</pre></Body><div Class="container-fluid" Style="background-color:#343a40"  ><footer ><div Class="container-fluid"  ><div Class="row align-items-center"  ><div Class="col-md"  ><p ><a Target="_self" Class="btn-sm btn btn-outline-success" href="#"  >I ♥ PS ></a></p></div><div Class="col-md"  ><p >Based on <a Target="_blank" href="https://www.powershellgallery.com/packages/Pode"  >pode</a> and <a Target="_blank" href="https://www.powershellgallery.com/packages/PSHTML"  >PSHTML</a></p></div><div Class="col-md" Style="color:#000"  ><p >Created at 2024-08-18 12:13:55</p></div></div></div></footer></div></html>
